{"stage": "review", "action": "scientific_findings", "result": {"verdict": "revise", "findings": ["The 'Scaling off changes weights' test asserts panels.2 (scaled scores Z) equals 9 and 0, but panels.2 holds Z = S/denom; with scale off denom=1 so Z=S=[9,0]. The test's expected values are actually the softmax weights (panels.2 is misindexed — it should target panels.2 for scores but the values 9/0 are scores, while actual 0.9998/0.0001 are weights). The test is internally inconsistent: it labels the path panels.2.values but expects weight-like numbers. Fix the test to assert panels.2.values.0.0=9 and panels.2.values.0.1=0 (raw scores), which the compute actually produces.", "The 'Score variance (theory)' metric hardcodes value=dk regardless of the actual Q,K entries, so it does not change when the learner edits Q or K. It is a theoretical annotation, not a computed output; it should be labeled as such or computed from the actual data (e.g. sample variance of the dot products) so that meaningful input changes affect it. As written it is a constant that misleads learners into thinking it reflects their matrices.", "The 'Max |row sum - 1|' metric and row-sum bar panel are computed from A, which is correct, but the metric is placed at metrics.2 while the identity test asserts metrics.2.value=0 — that is consistent. However the equal-scores exploration claims 'every entry of A becomes 0.5' for Q=[[1,0],[1,0]], K=[[1,0],[1,0]]: with scaling on, S=[[1,1],[1,1]], Z=[[0.707,0.707],[0.707,0.707]], softmax gives 0.5 each — correct. No issue there."], "reference_tests": [{"name": "Scaling off raw scores equal dot products", "state": {"Q": [[3, 0]], "K": [[3, 0], [0, 1]], "V": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "scale": false}, "expect": [{"path": "panels.0.values.0.0", "value": 9, "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "panels.0.values.0.1", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "panels.1.values.0.0", "value": 9, "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "panels.1.values.0.1", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-08}]}, {"name": "Scaling on divides scores by sqrt(dk)", "state": {"Q": [[3, 0]], "K": [[3, 0], [0, 1]], "V": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "scale": true}, "expect": [{"path": "panels.1.values.0.0", "formula": "9/Math.sqrt(2)", "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "panels.1.values.0.1", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-08}]}, {"name": "Output equals weighted sum of V rows (edge: dominant key)", "state": {"Q": [[3, 0]], "K": [[3, 0], [0, 1]], "V": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "scale": false}, "expect": [{"path": "panels.3.values.0.0", "formula": "(()=>{const z=[9,0];const m=Math.max(...z);const e=z.map(x=>Math.exp(x-m));const s=e.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);const a=e.map(x=>x/s);return a[0]*1+a[1]*0;})()", "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "panels.3.values.0.1", "formula": "(()=>{const z=[9,0];const m=Math.max(...z);const e=z.map(x=>Math.exp(x-m));const s=e.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);const a=e.map(x=>x/s);return a[0]*0+a[1]*1;})()", "atol": 1e-08}]}], "invariants": [{"name": "Each attention weight row sums to 1", "expression": "o.panels[2].values.every(r=>Math.abs(r.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)-1)<1e-9)"}, {"name": "Output row equals weighted sum of V rows", "expression": "o.panels[3].values.every((row,i)=>row.every((val,c)=>Math.abs(val-s.V.reduce((acc,v,j)=>acc+o.panels[2].values[i][j]*v[c],0))<1e-9))"}]}, "elapsed_seconds": 44.997}
